## Bugfix #1: Vector Dimension Mismatch (CRITICAL)

> [!CAUTION]
> The `gemini-embedding-001` model outputs **3072-dimensional** vectors, but our `golden_resume_bullets` table and `match_golden_bullets` RPC were created with `VECTOR(768)`. This caused every single insert to fail. Zero golden bullets were saved.

### Fix

#### [MODIFY] Supabase SQL — Run in SQL Editor

```sql
-- Drop the old table and recreate with correct dimensions
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS match_golden_bullets;
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS golden_resume_bullets_embedding_idx;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS golden_resume_bullets;

CREATE TABLE golden_resume_bullets (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  bullet_text TEXT NOT NULL,
  resume_source TEXT NOT NULL,
  company_placed TEXT,
  target_role TEXT DEFAULT 'consulting',   -- NEW: role tagging
  section_type TEXT NOT NULL,
  structural_skeleton TEXT NOT NULL,
  action_verb TEXT,
  has_metrics BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
  metric_type TEXT,
  quality_tier TEXT DEFAULT 'gold',
  embedding VECTOR(3072),                   -- FIXED: 3072 dimensions
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX ON golden_resume_bullets USING ivfflat (embedding vector_cosine_ops) WITH (lists = 20);

ALTER TABLE golden_resume_bullets ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Public read for golden_resume_bullets" ON golden_resume_bullets FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Service role insert for golden_resume_bullets" ON golden_resume_bullets FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (true);

-- Recreate the RPC with role filtering
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION match_golden_bullets (
  query_embedding VECTOR(3072),
  match_count INT DEFAULT 3,
  filter_section_type TEXT DEFAULT NULL,
  filter_target_role TEXT DEFAULT NULL
) RETURNS TABLE (
  id UUID,
  bullet_text TEXT,
  structural_skeleton TEXT,
  action_verb TEXT,
  section_type TEXT,
  company_placed TEXT,
  target_role TEXT,
  similarity FLOAT
)
LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $func$
BEGIN
  RETURN QUERY
  SELECT
    g.id, g.bullet_text, g.structural_skeleton, g.action_verb,
    g.section_type, g.company_placed, g.target_role,
    1 - (g.embedding <=> query_embedding) AS similarity
  FROM golden_resume_bullets g
  WHERE (filter_section_type IS NULL OR g.section_type = filter_section_type)
    AND (filter_target_role IS NULL OR g.target_role = filter_target_role)
  ORDER BY g.embedding <=> query_embedding
  LIMIT match_count;
END;
$func$;
```

#### [MODIFY] `apps/api/agents/resume_analyzer.py`
- Update the `embed_text` function. The current code uses `genai.embed_content(model='models/gemini-embedding-001', ...)`. This returns 3072-dim vectors which now matches the fixed table.

#### [MODIFY] `apps/api/scripts/process_resumes.py`
- Add a `target_role` field to each insert (detected from the subfolder name, e.g., `consult` → `consulting`, `finance` → `finance`).
- Change the script to scan **all subfolders** under `data/resumes/`, not just `consult/`.

